  "body": "### What is the expected enhancement?\n\n#667 tracks the implementation of a specific method of what this issue implies, but this issue is actually a requirement before #667 can be tackled.\r\n\r\nThe [current `FermionicOp`](https://github.com/Qiskit/qiskit-nature/blob/ce3e8a58dfd0306ccc41ddc9ff7b78050999cc62/qiskit_nature/second_q/operators/fermionic_op.py) should be able to serve as a decent guide in combination with the existing `SpinOp` to tackle this issue.\r\nOnly sparse labels should be supported.\r\n\r\nCare must be taken in this scenario, because the `SpinOp` carries additional data in the form of the spin associated with the operator.\r\n#515 should also be kept in mind when refactoring this operator (it does not need to be solved immediately since that also requires changes to the mappers) but it would be worthwhile to think whether we want direct support inside of `SpinOp` or whether we want to handle this via for example a #795.",
